{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T16:56:10.233Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1726+pm-gh1727+pm-gh1728+pm-gh1729","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T16:56:10.233Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-14T16:56:10.232Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause (2026-11-14): PmCompleteListValidationError built a fixed recovery (pm list ... --no-truncate ... and await client.listAllComplete()) with no knowledge of the request, so a refused includeBody request was retried without bodies. Fix: the constructor takes PmCompleteListOptions; certifyCompleteListResult and assertCompleteListResult take an optional options argument, and without it read the candidate's own filters.include_body record (every list envelope carries it when bodies were requested). listAllComplete passes its options through. The recovery drops the redundant legacy --no-truncate alias because --output-limit unbounded --output-budget unbounded already cover it."}]}],"before_hash":"ea9e447e237ef4c90a10d3ef1a7073d285af6a4f80a804e7ec85b419658cefe3","after_hash":"23a5e84bf56641e069df8c954d4fcc4482878765018a047c08e8c6a970659c60","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"217a7e7ed26ad4cef1ac6bea0a7a118ca3c4a06216782b9f5c8a7350f9f4255b"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T17:19:50.102Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1726+pm-gh1727+pm-gh1728+pm-gh1729","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1726","claim:pm-gh1727","claim:pm-gh1728","claim:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-gh1729","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-14T17:19:50.100Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Correction (2026-11-14, same session): the recovery KEEPS --no-truncate. Executing the emitted retry without it against a fresh tracker returned 3/3 items with has_more false, yet certification refused it as page_incomplete, because inspectEnvelopeShape requires filters.no_truncate and pm list echoes that only for the legacy flag (src/sdk/query/list.ts); --no-truncate also lifts list's own default page limit (resolveListPageLimit caps an unlimited read at 20 rows on a tracker of 10,000+ items). So the alias is load-bearing, not redundant, and the issue's secondary request is declined with that evidence. The mismatch it exposes (the migration hint tells callers to replace --no-truncate with --output-limit unbounded --output-budget unbounded, which yields an uncertifiable list) is filed separately."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T17:19:50.102Z"}],"before_hash":"23a5e84bf56641e069df8c954d4fcc4482878765018a047c08e8c6a970659c60","after_hash":"2a29cb0d10af0d12ba3030552fb6d15ffbce1f36d77ad744ff434e99bdaaaf22","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8b184d53d538fde79d0c1fd900bac1ff646a1feb25b49037a089c43166c56f65"}
